      "risk_48h": null,
      "risk_7d": null,
      "next_update": null,
      "raw_text": "(1) THE AREA OF CONVECTION (INVEST 92B) PREVIOUSLY LOCATED NEAR \n8.3N 87.6E IS NOW LOCATED NEAR 6.5N 87.9E, APPROXIMATELY 395 NM \nSOUTHWEST OF PORT BLAIR. ANIMATED ENHANCED INFRARED SATELLITE IMAGERY \nDEPICTS INVEST 92B WITH A BROAD LOW-LEVEL CIRCULATION CENTER (LLCC) \nAND FLARING CONVECTION THROUGHOUT THE SOUTHERN PERIPHERY. \nENVIRONMENTAL ANALYSIS INDICATES A FAVORABLE ENVIRONMENT FOR \nDEVELOPMENT WITH LOW (10-15 KTS) VERTICAL WIND SHEAR, MODERATE RADIAL \nOUTFLOW ALOFT, AND WARM SEA SURFACE TEMPERATURES (29-30C). GLOBAL \nDETERMINISTIC AND ENSEMBLE MODELS DEPICT GRADUAL DEVELOPMENT OVER THE \nNEXT 48 HOURS AS THE SYSTEM TRANSITS NORTHWESTWARD. MAXIMUM SUSTAINED \nSURFACE WINDS ARE ESTIMATED AT 23 TO 28 KNOTS. MINIMUM SEA LEVEL \nPRESSURE IS ESTIMATED TO BE NEAR 1008 MB. THE POTENTIAL FOR THE \nDEVELOPMENT OF A SIGNIFICANT TROPICAL CYCLONE WITHIN THE NEXT 24 \nHOURS REMAINS LOW. SEE REF A () FOR FURTHER DETAILS.",
